== Problem description ==
<!-- 
Provide a concise description of the issue here. Be  as specific as possible to help readers quickly determine whether or not this is the exact problem they are facing.
 -->

Wi-Fi is not working or cannot be enabled. The device fails to detect or connect to wireless networks despite no visible board damage.

== Symptoms ==
<!--
Detail all measurable or observable symptoms in this section. 
-->
* Unable to turn on wifi
[[File:Unable to turn on wifi note 10 lite.png|center|thumb|UNABLE TO TURN ON WIFI]]
* Stuck on faded blue color(depended on theme of the phone)
[[File:NOTE 10 LITE WIFI LIST NOT LOADING.png|center|thumb|WIFI LIST NOT LOADING]]
* No wifi list showing in the settings
* Bluetooth doesn't turn on aswell

== Solution ==
<!-- 
If the issue has a single, specific solution, provide it in this section and delete the sub-headers below. Otherwise, if there are multiple potential causes for the problem, outline the process of identifying the root cause and offer corresponding solutions below.

-->

There are three main reasons on this specific device the wifi and the bluetooth stops turning on:
[[File:WIFI IC LOCATION NOTE 10 LITE.png|center|thumb|WIFI IC LOCATION]]

[[File:Diode value under wifi galaxy note 10 lite.png|center|thumb|DIODE VALUE UNDER IC]]

# Cold solder under wfi ic:
## Check for any physical damage near the wifi ic
## Check for shorts near the wifi ic
## Remove the wifi ic
## Check diode value under the wifi ic
## If all diode readings are normal, reball and resolder the Wi-Fi IC, then test if the issue is resolved.
# Bad Wifi Ic: 
## If there is no change after reballing, replace the Wi-Fi IC with a known-good IC from a donor board
## If still doesn't work try to retrace the OL pads to see for any open lines
# Cpu Problem: 
## If you get any open line from CPU side proceed to reball the CPU
## In some cases, all signal lines between the CPU and the Wi-Fi IC may test good, but Wi-Fi functionality will still does not work.
## The solution to this is if you tried all the above is to reball a CPU
